# Anchor / cargo build output.
target/
.anchor/

# `fixtures/` is deliberately NOT ignored. `aera_v0_1.so` is the previously
# deployed program and the migration suite replays real v0.1 account state
# through the current one; this repository has no history from before v0.2, so
# it cannot be rebuilt here and has to be committed. `aera_v0_2.so` is the
# current program, rebuilt by build-artifacts.sh before every run -- committed
# only because tests/common/mod.rs pulls both in with `include_bytes!`, which
# resolves at compile time, so without it `cargo clippy --all-targets` does not
# build on a fresh clone.
#
# MANIFEST.txt is the exception: it is a report of one run, written by
# build-artifacts.sh and read straight back by test.sh to print step 7. Nothing
# reads a committed copy, and a committed copy is stale the moment anyone
# builds -- it would sit in the repository looking like a statement of what the
# artifacts hash to, while naming whichever machine wrote it last. The hash
# that is actually enforced is V0_1_EXPECTED_HASHES in
# tools/build-artifacts.sh, which is code and is committed.
fixtures/MANIFEST.txt

# Anchor writes the deploy keypair here on a local build. It is a signing key.
**/*-keypair.json

node_modules/
.DS_Store
